WEBVTT

00:06.820 --> 00:08.980
Hey, I brought some pajamas.

00:08.980 --> 00:11.240
Hey! Hold on! I'm naked in here!

00:11.240 --> 00:15.490
Settle down, princess. There's 
too much steam to see anything.

00:15.780 --> 00:17.240
You'd better be telling the truth.

00:17.240 --> 00:18.380
I'm not.

00:18.380 --> 00:20.370
Aw, come on!

00:22.590 --> 00:26.960
A whole lot has happened over 
these two years, huh, Sylvie?

00:26.960 --> 00:30.970
<i>Yep. You and I have both gotten bigger.</i>

00:30.970 --> 00:32.130
That's true.

00:32.540 --> 00:34.130
Are you going to take a shower, too?

00:34.130 --> 00:35.390
I think I will.

00:36.420 --> 00:39.060
You were gone for a long 
time, what were you doing?

00:39.060 --> 00:42.930
Had some things I needed 
Uncle Vincent's help with.

00:43.670 --> 00:46.450
Plus, I asked him about 
providing financial assistance

00:46.450 --> 00:48.150
for your Xyrus Academy tuition.

00:48.150 --> 00:50.910
Really? What'd he say?!

00:51.410 --> 00:52.400
"Of course!"

00:52.680 --> 00:56.140
You're gonna leave me with just that?!

02:28.880 --> 02:33.900
#10 The King Negotiates.

02:28.910 --> 02:31.990
You think we're gonna learn all kinds 
of stuff once we're in the academy?

02:32.530 --> 02:36.010
It's supposed to be the uncontested, 
number one magic academy, right?

02:36.010 --> 02:41.010
We should still have more technical 
knowledge than most first-years.

02:41.240 --> 02:44.190
They're bound to have a bunch 
of famous families attending.

02:44.190 --> 02:46.070
The idea that exchanging advice with them

02:46.070 --> 02:51.450
might help me get my power 
under control is really exciting!

02:52.270 --> 02:57.780
I'd like to learn more about my 
lightning and ice elemental magic.

02:58.250 --> 03:02.850
Lightning burns through mana 
quickly and is hard to control.

03:02.850 --> 03:07.370
And ice is hard to control even 
when tapping into my Beast Will.

03:07.580 --> 03:11.580
I'm curious... Have you thought about
what you're gonna do about Lucas?

03:11.940 --> 03:14.640
Even if I got revenge on him,

03:14.640 --> 03:18.250
I don't think I'd be able to withstand 
the reprisals from his family.

03:18.250 --> 03:20.590
So, for now, I just intend to get stronger.

03:20.890 --> 03:25.100
I'm shocked you can resist going 
after that piece of trash.

03:25.330 --> 03:26.440
Well, yeah.

03:27.040 --> 03:30.600
But I was more surprised when you 
made a wall between us with pillows.

03:30.600 --> 03:34.980
Of course I did! Sleeping in 
the same bed is just weird!

03:36.160 --> 03:38.090
Would you have preferred if I was a girl?

03:38.090 --> 03:39.490
Shut up, stupid!

03:43.060 --> 03:45.740
Do you think I'll be able to get 
a girlfriend at the academy?

03:46.170 --> 03:50.250
For someone who acts so serious, 
your worries are pretty normal.

03:50.480 --> 03:52.500
I know you're thinking 
about it, too, Arthur.

03:52.800 --> 03:57.710
Don't worry. I'm sure you'll run into a 
nice girl with black hair and glasses.

03:58.330 --> 04:00.630
You'll end up marrying her,

04:00.630 --> 04:03.510
and the two of you will have an adorable 
baby with black hair, and glasses.

04:03.800 --> 04:07.110
No baby is born wearing glasses.

04:07.110 --> 04:10.410
I bet with those irritating 
princely looks,

04:10.410 --> 04:13.020
you'll manage to get a girl 
with no trouble at all.

04:13.020 --> 04:14.440
Are you a little jealous?

04:14.440 --> 04:16.270
You really think "little" covers it?

04:16.270 --> 04:20.830
It'll be okay, glasses. 
I'm not really interested in girls.

04:25.080 --> 04:26.760
Anyway, let's hurry up and sleep.

04:27.640 --> 04:29.470
Yeah. Goodnight.

04:36.010 --> 04:37.540
Oh, what a relief.

04:37.820 --> 04:38.680
You're up.

04:38.680 --> 04:40.050
Good morning.

04:40.310 --> 04:43.370
I recalled how you mentioned 
wanting to talk to an inventor.

04:43.370 --> 04:46.110
Well, I contacted a friend 
of mine this morning.

04:46.110 --> 04:47.430
Really?

04:47.910 --> 04:49.810
He's a fellow named Gideon.

04:49.810 --> 04:53.750
Remember how I hired you for that quest 
about capturing an aquatic mana beast?

04:53.750 --> 04:55.060
Yeah.

04:55.060 --> 04:58.100
He was the one who actually needed it.

04:58.430 --> 05:01.900
He's an eminent researcher and 
probably the most talented

05:01.900 --> 05:03.580
inventor and engineer in Sapin.

05:05.540 --> 05:08.850
I'm curious, were you hoping 
to procure something from him?

05:08.850 --> 05:10.450
Well, basically.

05:10.740 --> 05:13.200
<i>A birthday present for Elanor.</i>

05:13.200 --> 05:14.430
Arthur?

05:14.430 --> 05:17.460
There you are! And with Vincent.

05:17.460 --> 05:21.160
Huh? Should you really 
be standing around here?

05:21.160 --> 05:24.070
I thought you had a meeting 
with someone this morning.

05:24.070 --> 05:25.840
That's right!

05:25.840 --> 05:27.340
Well, I need to go!

05:27.580 --> 05:30.430
Watch where you're going 
so you don't fall, old man!

05:30.780 --> 05:33.600
Speaking of old men,\hhow's your training going?

05:33.600 --> 05:38.520
Well, your old man happens to have 
officially hit the orange stage!

05:39.170 --> 05:40.990
Which reminded me of something.

05:40.990 --> 05:46.860
For some reason, this beast core didn't 
crumble after I absorbed mana from it.

05:48.550 --> 05:51.740
Which is why, once you're ready,
 we're heading out.

05:56.330 --> 05:57.870
<i>Something strange is going on.</i>

06:01.380 --> 06:03.300
<i>Why didn't it crumble?</i>

06:18.910 --> 06:21.650
<i>There's a Beast Will inside of the core?!</i>

06:22.460 --> 06:27.650
<i>Obtaining a Beast Will means the 
beast surrendering it willingly,</i>

06:27.650 --> 06:31.960
<i>or a human seizing it 
from the beast core.</i>

06:33.080 --> 06:37.660
<i>What would happen if I tried 
to combine two beasts?</i>

06:37.950 --> 06:40.830
<i>Perhaps the question should be,
 is that even possible?</i>

06:41.450 --> 06:44.440
<i>There's only one way to find out.</i>

07:13.940 --> 07:17.480
<i>Any longer and my dragon's 
will would have crushed</i>

07:17.480 --> 07:20.710
<i>the Elder Wood guardian spirit's will.</i>

07:22.610 --> 07:26.840
I wonder why Dad couldn't 
absorb the Beast Will?

07:27.170 --> 07:31.680
The elemental alignment of the beast and 
that of the mage must be compatible!

07:31.680 --> 07:34.090
Make sure to remember that!

07:34.310 --> 07:36.360
Oh, that's right.

07:38.040 --> 07:40.980
<i>I know the perfect person to give this to.</i>

07:44.220 --> 07:46.430
<i>I wonder how she's doing.</i>

07:56.880 --> 08:00.750
Good morning, Arthur.
Mom says breakfast is ready.

08:01.010 --> 08:04.750
I want that fancy dimension ring.

08:04.750 --> 08:09.880
There's a big announcement today, so 
Mom says to hurry up and get ready.

08:11.030 --> 08:12.760
What big announcement?

08:12.760 --> 08:14.460
Did you forget?

08:14.460 --> 08:17.570
The royalty of Sapin, Elenoir, 
and Darv are getting together

08:17.570 --> 08:19.620
to make some announcement,

08:19.620 --> 08:23.270
and it's going to be broadcast in 
the square, downtown. Remember?

08:23.270 --> 08:25.800
Oh, right.

08:27.510 --> 08:30.030
So, how about it, my sweet big brother?

08:33.320 --> 08:39.540
E-Eleanor... you're too big 
to still be doing that.

08:39.540 --> 08:42.120
Get ready and head downstairs already.

08:42.120 --> 08:45.290
Mom and I are going out 
with Aunt Tabitha.

08:46.950 --> 08:50.420
Where did she get that violent side from?

08:50.990 --> 08:53.550
I think I know.

08:55.770 --> 08:58.150
I'm still hungry.

08:58.150 --> 08:59.300
I bet.

08:59.650 --> 09:02.810
Considering how much Sylvie has 
been stealing from your plate.

09:02.810 --> 09:04.310
Tell me about it.

09:04.600 --> 09:07.560
Well, while you're meeting 
with the inventor,

09:07.560 --> 09:10.070
I'm going to wander around the shops.

09:10.610 --> 09:13.570
You actually have enough 
money to go shopping?

09:13.570 --> 09:18.290
Unlike someone, I actually save 
the money I earn in dungeons.

09:18.290 --> 09:20.080
Well, good for you.

09:20.680 --> 09:23.450
Sylvie, help Elijah with his shopping.

09:28.610 --> 09:31.590
<i>Can't have Gideon getting 
curious about her.</i>

09:34.490 --> 09:35.460
Is this the place?

09:35.460 --> 09:36.340
It is.

09:37.840 --> 09:40.470
Master Gideon is out at the moment...

09:40.470 --> 09:41.600
Mr. Vincent!

09:41.600 --> 09:43.570
Good to see you again, Himes.

09:43.570 --> 09:45.600
Please, come in.

09:46.200 --> 09:47.470
Right this way.

09:48.390 --> 09:49.610
Sir!

09:49.610 --> 09:52.860
Himes! I told you to 
not let anyone in here!

09:54.150 --> 09:57.610
Oh, it's you. Come to interrupt me again?

09:57.610 --> 10:00.370
I let you know I was coming.

10:00.370 --> 10:03.790
I've been getting more and more 
frustrated with seeing people, lately.

10:03.790 --> 10:05.040
Which is probably due to

10:05.040 --> 10:07.370
the royals sending 10 or 20 messengers 
my way over the last year,

10:07.370 --> 10:11.880
pestering me about finding a way to 
enable long-distance trips over the sea.

10:11.880 --> 10:15.880
Long-distance sea trips? What for?

10:15.880 --> 10:17.760
None of your business, that's what.

10:19.130 --> 10:21.890
Hang on. Who is this boy, anyway?

10:22.110 --> 10:24.890
It's an honor to meet you, Gideon.

10:25.280 --> 10:30.280
Uncle Vincent has told me all 
about how incredible you are.

10:30.280 --> 10:33.900
My name is Arthur Leywin, 
and I'm Reynold's son.

10:33.900 --> 10:37.420
You know I'm not in the market for 
a student or apprentice, Vincent.

10:37.420 --> 10:39.660
So, why is this child here?

10:39.970 --> 10:43.560
I was hoping to find 
out myself, actually.

10:44.160 --> 10:48.830
I was going to show you an interesting 
idea for an invention I had, but...

10:48.830 --> 10:53.420
You mentioned needing a way to 
make long-distance trips by sea?

10:55.830 --> 10:57.920
I guess I can use that.

10:59.920 --> 11:04.300
I get the feeling it'd be faster 
to show you than explain.

11:05.190 --> 11:08.740
I have no idea what you 
intend on doodling,

11:08.740 --> 11:11.940
but no child could come up with a 
solution to the problem that I'm—

11:12.180 --> 11:17.440
What?! Where did you get this from?! 
And... could it really...

11:17.440 --> 11:18.360
Give me that!

11:19.210 --> 11:20.900
Instead of using mana as fuel,

11:20.900 --> 11:25.560
an engine that moves from steam that 
is created with other resources.

11:25.560 --> 11:27.800
How did it not occur to me?!

11:27.800 --> 11:32.080
Hang on. This part doesn't make sense.
 It's missing something.

11:32.830 --> 11:37.710
I left out some crucial details, 
which I'll be happy to tell you about.

11:38.210 --> 11:42.220
Assuming our negotiations go well.

11:42.220 --> 11:43.220
Boy...

11:43.220 --> 11:45.970
You're no mere child, are you?

11:46.230 --> 11:47.090
No matter.

11:50.730 --> 11:55.480
I'm sure any of my random creations 
would be enough to shock you,

11:55.480 --> 11:58.480
but use those clear blue 
eyes to behold this!

12:01.990 --> 12:05.490
A gem of the highest quality you'll 
find anywhere on the continent!

12:05.770 --> 12:08.860
It can absorb five times 
the typical amount of mana.

12:08.860 --> 12:12.660
Vincent has told me you're 
something of a fledgling mage.

12:12.660 --> 12:14.750
I never called him a fledgling.

12:15.640 --> 12:19.250
That's impressive. 
But it's not something I need.

12:19.600 --> 12:22.010
You don't?! Very well!

12:22.280 --> 12:26.010
Himes, bring the items from the 
middle of row C! All of them!

12:26.300 --> 12:30.770
No one else has seen these before, 
but I'm making an exception for you.

12:31.060 --> 12:34.360
This mirror can refract light 
so powerfully that five—

12:33.520 --> 12:35.520
Not interested.

12:35.520 --> 12:36.530
How about this?

12:36.530 --> 12:37.660
No, thank you.

12:36.840 --> 12:43.030
<i>Being able to stand up to the infamous 
Gideon... That's Arthur for you. But...</i>

12:37.660 --> 12:39.160
Surely you can't resist this.

12:39.160 --> 12:40.030
I can.

12:40.030 --> 12:41.860
This then? I know you'll love it!

12:41.860 --> 12:43.030
No, not really.

12:43.030 --> 12:45.530
Just take something already, blast it!

12:46.090 --> 12:49.790
<i>I'm not sure I understand what's 
unfolding before my eyes.</i>

12:49.790 --> 12:52.790
You're really not leaving 
me with much of a choice.

12:53.160 --> 12:56.160
Himes! Bring the pendants!

12:56.160 --> 12:59.290
But, Master, those are special...

12:59.290 --> 13:00.550
I realize that!

13:00.550 --> 13:01.620
Bring them anyway!

13:01.620 --> 13:04.050
R-Right. Very good, sir.

13:06.300 --> 13:08.280
I had the finest jewlers to design

13:08.280 --> 13:10.560
something of sublime beauty.

13:10.560 --> 13:13.350
They're fit for a royal, I'd say!

13:15.370 --> 13:17.980
They were made from a phoenix wyrm.

13:18.240 --> 13:20.140
Indeed they are.

13:20.140 --> 13:22.610
Wait! How did you know that?!

13:23.190 --> 13:24.240
What even is that?

13:24.500 --> 13:30.510
An S-rank mana beast that's 
as rare as a dragon,

13:30.510 --> 13:33.140
with unique survival abilities.

13:34.230 --> 13:39.000
If I had to guess, he found a way to 
transfer that power to the pendant.

13:39.000 --> 13:40.250
Right you are!

13:40.530 --> 13:41.890
When faced with danger,

13:41.890 --> 13:45.780
much like how phoenix wyrms 
will preserve their own lives,

13:45.780 --> 13:50.380
these pendants will encase the 
wearer with a defensive barrier.

13:50.770 --> 13:53.010
But that's not the impressive part.

13:53.250 --> 13:58.400
Should the protective barrier be broken,
the mana stored in the pendants

13:58.400 --> 14:02.270
will transport the wearer
 to the safest place possible.

14:02.270 --> 14:03.530
How's that?

14:03.530 --> 14:06.530
And how many times will that effect work?

14:06.530 --> 14:08.030
Twice!

14:08.330 --> 14:11.000
To be perfectly honest, 
I'm not quite sure.

14:11.000 --> 14:13.910
But I would theorize twice.

14:14.390 --> 14:18.420
<i>These pendants might be good 
gifts for Eleanor and Mom.</i>

14:19.140 --> 14:20.170
Hang on.

14:20.500 --> 14:24.580
You mentioned you made 
this for royalty, right?

14:24.580 --> 14:27.920
That's right. A core was 
donated with that intent.

14:27.920 --> 14:30.090
And you'd give it away?

14:30.090 --> 14:31.680
More importantly...

14:31.680 --> 14:37.180
I'm curious how you came upon this idea, 
and why you chose to reveal it now.

14:37.180 --> 14:38.690
What are you after?!

14:38.980 --> 14:43.090
I just wanted to get a wonderful 
birthday present for my sister.

14:43.090 --> 14:44.440
Don't lie, boy!

14:44.440 --> 14:47.660
Besides, I can't really explain 
anything until you explain to me

14:47.660 --> 14:49.950
what the engine is for.

14:49.950 --> 14:54.950
Well, you'll understand soon enough, 
after the upcoming announcement.

14:55.260 --> 14:57.850
I'd imagine someone of your high standing

14:57.850 --> 15:00.000
would be privy to specifics that

15:00.000 --> 15:02.460
won't be included in the 
announcement for the public.

15:02.460 --> 15:08.720
All right, fine. But if I tell you,
I don't think you'll need the pendants.

15:08.720 --> 15:11.220
I'm not that much of a nice guy.

15:11.520 --> 15:14.970
In that case, instead 
of two, how about one?

15:16.220 --> 15:17.970
F-Fine, fine!

15:18.260 --> 15:19.730
<i>You devil!</i>

15:19.950 --> 15:22.090
I might not understand 
everything that goes on

15:22.090 --> 15:23.910
in that genius brain of Arthur's,

15:24.270 --> 15:30.240
but he always keeps his word. 
You can be sure of that.

15:30.240 --> 15:36.240
Fine, fine! My number one priority 
is creating this vessel!

15:36.690 --> 15:39.780
Some time last year...

15:39.780 --> 15:43.630
we confirmed the existence of another 
continent, other than Dicathen.

15:43.860 --> 15:46.380
A new continent?

15:46.650 --> 15:48.770
Then the rumors were true!

15:48.770 --> 15:51.380
You knew, Uncle Vincent?

15:51.380 --> 15:55.390
Some of the folks who serve 
the royals have loose lips.

15:56.030 --> 16:01.140
I wasn't sure if it was true or not. 
But right now it seems a lot more feasible.

16:01.390 --> 16:02.650
Is there any evidence?

16:02.650 --> 16:05.900
Only a mad scientist would make
 such a claim without evidence!

16:07.690 --> 16:10.620
Two or three years ago, 
a bird-like mana beast

16:10.620 --> 16:13.370
previously unknown 
in Dicathen was discovered.

16:13.370 --> 16:16.060
It had the ability to blend almost 
completely into its surroundings;

16:16.060 --> 16:18.910
a rather incredible form of camouflage.

16:19.180 --> 16:22.440
A flying mana beast that 
can hide like that?

16:22.440 --> 16:24.420
I'm amazed someone was able to capture it.

16:24.690 --> 16:27.340
An adventurer stumbled onto it.

16:27.340 --> 16:29.780
The creature was wearing with
 an incredibly complicated device.

16:29.780 --> 16:34.430
I only was able to decipher its 
functionality in the last year.

16:34.430 --> 16:37.930
What kind of device was it?

16:37.930 --> 16:39.930
Do you realize what you're asking?

16:39.930 --> 16:42.860
We're talking about the kind 
of top secret information

16:42.860 --> 16:44.260
that's only available to royalty!

16:44.260 --> 16:49.190
Then I suppose the blueprint engine 
is an even higher level of secrecy.

16:49.190 --> 16:51.440
After all, even royalty 
doesn't know about it.

16:51.760 --> 16:55.700
It was a machine cable of 
recording and store moving images.

16:55.700 --> 16:56.950
Is that all?

16:56.950 --> 16:58.320
You little brat!

16:58.320 --> 16:59.850
There's more to it than that!

16:59.850 --> 17:03.240
Recordings from all three kingdoms 
had been captured in detail!

17:03.240 --> 17:08.710
We can assume that wherever it came from 
is a land with many powerful mages!

17:08.710 --> 17:10.210
That settles it.

17:10.490 --> 17:12.440
We'll use the steam engine

17:12.440 --> 17:16.370
to travel to this new continent 
and see what's there.

17:18.050 --> 17:22.720
So, you were looking to get a 
birthday present for Eleanor?

17:22.980 --> 17:27.160
More or less. I was hoping to get her 
something nobody had ever seen before.

17:27.600 --> 17:31.230
I see. And the steam engine?

17:31.470 --> 17:35.360
<i>I don't think I'll share that 
it's knowledge from my past life.</i>

17:35.360 --> 17:39.990
It was just an idea I had 
 that happened to come in handy.

17:40.270 --> 17:41.990
You really are something.

17:42.270 --> 17:45.770
<i>Still, the existence of another 
continent apart from Dicathen...</i>

17:45.770 --> 17:47.000
Arthur!

17:51.730 --> 17:54.850
I'm so excited to hear the announcement.

17:54.850 --> 17:59.550
Elder Radius mentioned the three 
kingdoms have been discussing merging.

18:02.640 --> 18:05.770
Isn't that a student from Xyrus Academy?

18:05.770 --> 18:10.400
It's bad enough there's a 
dwarf attending our school,

18:11.650 --> 18:14.810
but he doesn't seem to realize that 
practicing magic outside of school

18:14.810 --> 18:16.370
is again the rules, too.

18:16.370 --> 18:19.030
You're trying to use mana to 
protect yourself, aren't you?

18:19.400 --> 18:20.830
Please... stop.

18:20.830 --> 18:22.510
Then put your mana away.

18:25.790 --> 18:28.040
I told you to put your mana away!

18:28.040 --> 18:30.060
That's enough!

18:31.790 --> 18:33.290
Are you okay? Can you stand?

18:33.640 --> 18:35.300
How can you do this?!

18:39.060 --> 18:41.550
You think you can interrupt my fun?

18:42.630 --> 18:48.810
<i>If I use magic here, it'll be causing 
trouble for Mr. Helstea and Arthur.</i>

18:50.170 --> 18:53.310
Hey, isn't that the emblem 
of the Darv kingdom?

18:53.690 --> 18:55.820
Now this is interesting!

18:56.210 --> 18:58.910
Were you hoping to get the 
same kind of treatment?

18:58.910 --> 19:01.880
Maybe share a hospital room 
with your friend here?

19:01.880 --> 19:03.700
Then the two of you can—

19:10.210 --> 19:14.710
Another commoner? 
I don't mind playing with you.

19:15.350 --> 19:16.710
That's great.

19:17.420 --> 19:20.180
I was really hoping we could 
have some fun together.

19:22.720 --> 19:24.720
A-Arthur...

19:25.110 --> 19:27.160
It's fine. Don't worry.

19:27.760 --> 19:29.230
Easier said than done.

19:29.560 --> 19:31.230
Leave this to me.

19:31.560 --> 19:33.230
I'll hit him once and he'll be—

19:38.860 --> 19:41.040
I wouldn't get full of yourself.

19:41.040 --> 19:44.870
There's a big difference between 
trained nobility and some commoner.

19:45.870 --> 19:49.780
Shocked?! This is a technique passed 
down through my family for generations,

19:49.780 --> 19:51.210
the 1,000 Step Attack!

19:51.710 --> 19:55.310
By swinging your weapon around, 
you confuse and distract your opponent.

19:55.310 --> 19:57.130
Then there's no way you can evade...

19:57.880 --> 20:00.880
my ultra super speed thrust!

20:04.630 --> 20:09.390
Aw, it broke. That tends to happen 
without mana reinforcement.

